cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AdaptiGuard: A Hash-Locked Evaluation Testbed for Runtime LLM-Agent Intervention Policies"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Do not cite it as a confirmed, SOTA, or production prompt-injection defense."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shirazi Matin
    given-names: Seyed Mohammadreza
    email: shirazimatin@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  AdaptiGuard is a hash-locked evaluation testbed for prompt-injection and
  related LLM-agent attacks, comparing fixed and adaptive discrete intervention
  policies under shared security, utility, and cost metrics. The VNEXT
  confirmation on pack vnext_confirm_v1.0 (61+61; SHA-256
  523c881820710783b5290c76ea5fe5fc01a6341fb427defcba1119fc3e721518) is a
  negative result (STATUS=FAIL): adaptive cost-aware intervention was not
  confirmed under the pre-registered MSID. Layer A remains a closed detector
  diagnostic. Workshop manuscript: docs/paper/workshop_vnext_fail/.
keywords:
  - LLM security
  - prompt injection
  - adaptive defense
  - negative result
  - evaluation framework
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohammadreza583/adapti-guard"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
